\b\par
Overview / Description\par
\b0\par
\pard\par
This is a much improved and more powerful version of Rob Storey's existing 'awsbrows.exe' utility (note spelling). Awsbrows.exe (withOUT the 'e') is Rob's program. AwsbrowsE.exe (WITH the 'e') is my own much more powerful version of the same thing.\par
\par
Rob's awsbrows is a handy utility (and until my AWSBrowse came along the only utility), but it was too lacking in features to be useful for my own purposes so I decided to write a better one.\par
\par
Among it's many features are:\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li810 Significantly faster than existing awsbrows.exe\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}More functional and user-friendly user-interface\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Supports both .aws and .het files, including spanned block files\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Supports both ZLIB and BZIP2 compressed het file formats (DLLs included), as well as Bus-Tech ZLIB compressed files too.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}User configurable hex display (font and layout)\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Hex/text search capability. Find whatever data you're looking for.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Displays both EBCDIC or ASCII\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Ditto-like toolbar buttons for quick positioning to next/previous block/file\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Detection/reporting of all Standard Labels\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Detailed tape summary statistics including StdLbl info\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}GoTo command for direct access to start of any StdLbl file\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Clipboard support for hex/text/binary data. Hex data copied from AWSBrowse can be pasted into Visual Studio's binary file editor.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Printing and Print Preview support (single selected blocks only)\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Supports large block sizes (greater than 64K)\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Supports extremely large files (greater than 4GB)\par
\pard\par
This is a must-have utility for anyone dealing with many AWS/HET files.\par
\par
\pard\qc\par
